<crash-analysis>
The crash is caused by a null pointer dereference in the `channel_free_all` function in `channels.c`. The `ssh->chanctxt` pointer, which is assigned to the local variable `sc`, is `NULL`. The code then attempts to access `sc->channels_alloc`, leading to a segmentation fault.

The fuzz driver calls `channel_free_all(ssh)` unconditionally at the end of its execution. It's possible for the fuzzer to generate inputs that do not lead to the allocation of any channels, in which case `ssh->chanctxt` might remain `NULL`. The `channel_free_all` function should be robust enough to handle this situation by simply returning if `ssh->chanctxt` is `NULL`, as there would be nothing to free.

Suggestion for patching the project:
Add a null check at the beginning of the `channel_free_all` function in `channels.c`:

```c
void
channel_free_all(struct ssh *ssh)
{
struct ssh_channels *sc = ssh->chanctxt;
u_int i;

if (sc == NULL)
return;

for (i = 0; i < sc->channels_alloc; i++) {
if (sc->channels[i] != NULL)
channel_free(ssh, sc->channels[i]);
}
free(sc->channels);
free(sc);
ssh->chanctxt = NULL;
}
```
</crash-analysis>

